        <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-primary/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-primary font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">3</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-white">Diplomacy was abandoned at the last minute</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mt-1">Oman announced a breakthrough on 27 February — Iran agreed to enrichment limits and IAEA verification. The strikes came the next day anyway.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle rounded-xl p-5">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-primary/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-primary font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">4</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-white">Nuclear program is the justification, regime change is the goal</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mt-1">Trump explicitly called on Iranians to "take over your government." The stated aim went beyond nuclear prevention to toppling the Islamic Republic.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle rounded-xl p-5">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-yellow-500/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-yellow-400 font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">5</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-white">Gulf states took direct hits</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mt-1">UAE, Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, and Jordan all sustained Iranian retaliatory strikes. Civilians were killed in the UAE and Syria. Airports were hit in Kuwait, Abu Dhabi, and Erbil.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle rounded-xl p-5">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-yellow-500/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-yellow-400 font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">6</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-white">Strait of Hormuz closure threatens the global economy</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mt-1">Iran's closure of the strait — through which 20% of the world's oil flows — has immediate implications for energy prices and global trade.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-bg-card border border-border-subtle rounded-xl p-5">
        <span class="w-8 h-8 bg-red-500/20 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-red-400 font-bold text-sm flex-shrink-0">7</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-medium text-white">The conflict is ongoing</h3>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mt-1">By 25 April 2026, the conflict had moved into a fragile ceasefire-and-blockade phase without a political settlement. After the 20 April 2026 seizure of the Iranian-flagged cargo ship Touska, diplomacy shifted away from the planned Oman track and into Pakistan-mediated indirect contacts. The Strait of Hormuz remained unstable, new US sanctions hit Iranian oil networks on 22 April 2026, Trump extended the ceasefire indefinitely on 24 April 2026 while threatening any Iranian mining effort, and Lebanon remained volatile despite a separate three-week truce extension announced on 24 April 2026. The region was no longer in the initial shock phase of war, but it remained an active, unresolved, high-risk crisis.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
